DMCA of the Bolivian league.

The exclusive broadcasting rights for the Bolivian First Division belong to the state-owned companyEntel Boliviaalong with theBolivian Football Federation (FBF).
Any retransmission, live signal distribution or use of images of local league matches (including the Entel Gol digital service ) that occurs without the express authorization of these entities is subject to copyright penalties and DMCA (Digital Millennium Copyright Act) takedown requests on internet platforms.
If you need to manage a claim or understand the league's content protection environment, consider the following points:

DMCA Monitoring and Reporting

• Signal Ownership:  Entel holds the absolute television and multiplatform (mobile and streaming) rights for the entire season. They, along with the FBF ( Bolivian Football Federation ), actively pursue pirated broadcasts on platforms such as Facebook, YouTube, Twitch, and illegal streaming websites by sending DMCA takedown notices.
• Legal precedents: The FBF has carried out audits and filed multimillion-dollar financial claims against operators who broadcast league matches without prior authorization, demonstrating a strict policy of protecting its intellectual property.
• Removal services: In Bolivia, there are agencies and law firms dedicated exclusively to managing copyright claims and removing infringing content from the web, such as DMCA Bolivia.

Once you've made changes, please reply to this message and let us know. If you don't tell us that you've made changes within the next 1 business day, we'll need to disable the entire repository according to our GitHub DMCA Takedown Policy:

https://docs.github.com/articles/dmca-takedown-policy/

If you believe your content on GitHub was mistakenly disabled by a DMCA takedown request, you have the right to contest the takedown by submitting a counter notice, as described in our DMCA Takedown Policy.
